## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over subsequences with a fixed length and pairwise costs, plus explicit reconstruction. It moves beyond contiguous partitions by requiring last-step linkage through prior picks.

## Key Concepts
- Subsequence DP with fixed length
- Min-over-predecessor recurrence
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and practical optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function solve(A, m){
  const n=A.length;
  const dp=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][1]=0;
  for(let t=2;t<=m;t++){
    for(let i=t-1;i<n;i++){
      for(let j=t-2;j<i;j++){
        const c=dp[j][t-1]+Math.abs(A[i]-A[j]);
        if(c<dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=c; par[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  let best=Infinity,bestI=-1;
  for(let i=m-1;i<n;i++){ if(dp[i][m]<best){ best=dp[i][m]; bestI=i; } }
  const path=[];
  let cur=bestI, t=m;
  while(t>=1){
    path.push(cur);
    cur=par[cur][t];
    t--;
  }
  path.reverse();
  return {cost:best, indices:path};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests DP with non-overlapping selections and per-subarray costs, mirroring real scenarios like batch processing, budget allocation, or ad-slot optimization where exactly k intervals are chosen from a sequence.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping k-interval DP
- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sum queries
- Maintaining a running best to optimize transitions from O(n) to O(1)
- Reconstruction of exact intervals

## DP Recurrence
Let pref[i] = sum of first i elements (pref[0] = 0).

**Transition:**
dp[i][t] = max(
  dp[i-1][t],                                    // Don't end a subarray at i
  best[t] + pref[i]                              // End a subarray at i
)

where best[t] = max_{1 ≤ l ≤ i} (dp[l-1][t-1] - pref[l-1])

**Initialization:**
dp[0][0] = 0, dp[0][t>0] = -∞

**Answer:** dp[n][k]

## Reconstruction
Track which choice was made at each dp[i][t]. If dp[i][t] came from dp[i-1][t], no subarray ends at i. Otherwise, find l where dp[l-1][t-1] - pref[l-1] = best[t], and record subarray (l..i).

## Complexity
- Time: O(nk) with O(1) transitions using running best
- Space: O(nk) for dp table, O(nk) for reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = [0];
  for (let x of A) pref.push(pref[pref.length - 1] + x);

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const choice = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      // Skip position i
      if (dp[i - 1][t] >= dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
        choice[i][t] = 0; // 0 = skip
      }

      // Start/extend subarray ending at i
      if (t > 0) {
        let best = -Infinity;
        for (let l = 1; l <= i; l++) {
          const val = dp[l - 1][t - 1] + (pref[i] - pref[l - 1]) - c;
          if (val > best) best = val;
        }
        if (best > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = best;
          choice[i][t] = 1; // 1 = take subarray ending at i
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruction
  const subarrays = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (i > 0 && t > 0) {
    if (choice[i][t] === 1) {
      let l = 1;
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = dp[j - 1][t - 1] + (pref[i] - pref[j - 1]) - c;
        if (val === dp[i][t]) {
          l = j;
          break;
        }
      }
      subarrays.unshift([l - 1, i - 1]); // Convert to 0-indexed
      t--;
    }
    i--;
  }

  return { value: dp[n][k], subarrays };
}
```

## Optimized O(nk) Version
The inner loop can be optimized by maintaining a running best:
```javascript
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    best[t] = Math.max(best[t], dp[i - 1][t - 1] - pref[i - 1]);
    dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][t], best[t] + pref[i] - c);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over partitioning with a non-trivial segment value (max letter value).

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions with exact k segments
- Precomputing segment values (maxChar)
- Reconstructing the cut points

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPartitionValue(s, k){
  const n = s.length;
  const val = [...s].map(c => c.charCodeAt(0) - 96); // a=1..z=26
  const maxChar = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(n+1).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    let m=0;
    for(let j=i;j<n;j++){
      m = Math.max(m, val[j]);
      maxChar[i][j+1] = m;
    }
  }
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const pre = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const cand = dp[p][t-1] + maxChar[p][i];
        if(cand > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = cand; pre[i][t] = p; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {value: dp[n][k], cuts: []};
}
```

